// Syncthing allowlist for the gold-annotation handoff.
//
// Code travels via git; only the private annotation data travels via Syncthing.
// Syncing .git/ across machines corrupts repos, and the venv (7.7G) and
// checkpoints (14G) are machine-specific -- so this file inverts the usual
// default: it admits a couple of paths and ignores everything else.
//
// ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING. Syncthing matches top-down, first match wins, and
// silently expands a bare directory pattern to cover its children too: `!/ml`
// also means `!/ml/**`. So a broad un-ignore placed too early re-admits the
// whole tree. Each level therefore goes: admit the payload, ignore the other
// children, THEN un-ignore the directory itself so Syncthing descends into it.
// Verify any edit with: GET /rest/db/ignores?folder=<id> and re-check
// localBytes on /rest/db/status -- it should stay ~50M, not 23G.

// -- ml/output: admit the payload, ignore the rest, then allow the dir --
!/ml/output/annotation
!/ml/output/splits
/ml/output/*
!/ml/output

// -- ml: ignore the other children (.venv, data, source), then allow the dir --
/ml/*
!/ml

// -- everything else in the repo, .git included --
*
